# Docker Compose: Always Use `-f docker-compose.prod.yml`

## The Problem

The production server has two compose files:

| File | Purpose | Backend `/app/data` mount |
|---|---|---|
| `docker-compose.yml` | Local development | `./data/bridge:/app/data:ro` (WRONG for backend) |
| `docker-compose.prod.yml` | Production server | `./data/backend:/app/data` (CORRECT, read-write) |

Running bare `docker compose up -d` uses `docker-compose.yml` by default, which mounts the bridge's data directory as read-only into the backend. This causes `session_memory` to fail with `[Errno 30] Read-only file system` and drops service health from 93/93 to 92/93.

## Rule

**Every `docker compose` command on the production server (68.183.168.75) MUST include `-f docker-compose.prod.yml`.**

```bash
# WRONG — uses docker-compose.yml, wrong volumes
docker compose up -d
docker compose up -d backend
docker compose restart backend

# CORRECT
docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d backend
docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml restart backend
```

## Key Differences Between Files

| Setting | `docker-compose.yml` | `docker-compose.prod.yml` |
|---|---|---|
| Backend `/app/data` | `data/bridge:ro` | `data/backend` (rw) |
| Backend `/app/scripts` | Not mounted | `./backend/scripts:/app/scripts:ro` (maintenance runners) |
| Bridge data cross-ref | Not available | `data/bridge:/app/bridge_data:ro` |
| Nginx container | Not included | Included (`nate_nginx`) |
| Health check deps | Basic | Full chain with `condition: service_healthy` |

## Stale Network Error

When switching between compose files or after partial stops, Docker may report:

```
Error response from daemon: error while removing network: network ... has active endpoints
```

Fix with:

```bash
docker network prune -f && docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d
```

## Backend scripts inside `nate_backend`

The prod backend image includes `COPY scripts/` and the compose file bind-mounts `./backend/scripts:/app/scripts:ro`. Run one-off Python tools **inside the container** so `DATABASE_URL`, `pgbouncer`, and `import app.*` match production:

```bash
# On GREEN from repo root — container already has DATABASE_URL via compose.
# Replace VAULT_PARENT with the directory that CONTAINS session_memories/ (discover first):
#   find /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab -type d -name session_memories | head -5
#   → parent of that path is --vault-root

docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml exec -T backend \
  python /app/scripts/backfill_classroom_session_analyses.py \
  --vault-root VAULT_PARENT \
  --classroom-sessions-file /app/data/classroom_sessions.json
```

Do **not** use `/app/scripts/...` until the bind mount exists (compose pulled + `backend` recreated). Do **not** pass a host-expanded `DATABASE_URL=...` through SSH quotes unless you intend that shell to substitute it—the container already has `DATABASE_URL` from compose.

## Verification After Any Compose Operation

```bash
# Confirm correct mount (must show data/backend, NOT data/bridge)
docker inspect nate_backend --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Destination}} -> {{.Source}} ({{.Mode}}){{println}}{{end}}' | grep /app/data

# Confirm scripts mount (optional)
docker inspect nate_backend --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{.Destination}} -> {{.Source}}{{"\n"}}{{end}}' | grep /app/scripts

# Confirm full health
docker logs nate_backend --since 30s 2>&1 | grep 'STARTUP COMPLETE'
# Expected: 116/116 services healthy — ALL SYSTEMS NOMINAL
```
